# UI verification

After changing routes, components, or global styles, run the browser smoke yourself. Do not ask the user to click unless you are blocked.

`pnpm test:e2e` is the pass/fail check for behavior. A screenshot is not a pass.

## Behavior

1. Convex is up. `pnpm dev` starts Vite on http://localhost:3213 and `convex dev` when that server is not already running.
2. The dev deployment may already have dishes. Run `pnpm exec convex run seed:seedDishes '{"householdId":"household-1"}'` only when `/library` has no dishes. Do not reseed on every UI change.
3. `pnpm test:e2e`

The command reuses `pnpm dev` on http://localhost:3213 when that server is already running. Otherwise it starts one. The spec is `e2e/app-smoke.spec.ts`. It opens the week plan, past plans (and one archived plan when a link is there), the recipe library, the shopping list, and history.

The stop hook allows you to finish only when this command passed for the current UI diff. Passing, then editing a UI file, means you run it again.

Add or extend a spec only when the task adds a new critical journey. Keep edge cases in Vitest.

## Layout and motion

For spacing, overflow, or motion, also drive real Chrome with the `user-chrome-devtools` tools:

1. Open the affected route.
2. Read console messages and fix errors.
3. Run `evaluate_script` for one fact (the text is present, the list has the expected count, or a panel is not clipped).
4. Save a screenshot under `.cursor/verification/<yyyy-mm-dd>-<slug>/` when the judgment is visual.

Do not use the Cursor built-in browser.

## Git

Do not `git add` or commit `test-results/`, `playwright-report/`, or `.cursor/verification/`.

## Completion report

State that `pnpm test:e2e` passed. For a visual change, also give the screenshot path and any console errors. If the server or Convex will not start, say what blocked you.
